      "source": [
        "# 2. Data audit, preparation and leakage control — Required Text Cell\n",
        "\n",
        "**Data dictionary.** `record_id` and `service_date` are identifiers/metadata and are never used\n",
        "as predictors. Numerical features describe weather (`avg_temperature_c`, `rainfall_mm`),\n",
        "operations (`scheduled_trips`, `completed_trips`, `avg_delay_min`, `breakdowns`,\n",
        "`incidents_last_30d`, `avg_speed_kmh`, `traffic_index`, `occupancy_rate`, `fuel_price_rwf_litre`)\n",
        "and vehicle sensors (`engine_temp_c`, `brake_temp_c`, `sensor_vibration_rms`,\n",
        "`sensor_accel_mean_g`, `gps_signal_quality`). Categorical features are `route_id`, `district`,\n",
        "`day_type`, `weather`, `road_condition`, `vehicle_type`. The continuous target is\n",
        "`passenger_demand`; the binary target is `high_risk` (recoded to `high_risk_binary`).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Data-quality issues found.** `weather` has 10 missing values and `avg_delay_min` has 12; there\n",
        "are 10 exact duplicate rows; `day_type`, `weather`, `district` and `vehicle_type` contain\n",
        "inconsistent casing/spacing (e.g. \"weekday\" vs \"Weekday\", \"RAINY\" vs \"Rainy\", \"mini bus\" vs\n",
        "\"Minibus\"); `road_condition` includes an explicit \"Unknown\" category; and `occupancy_rate`\n",
        "(max 1.28), `avg_speed_kmh` (max 145 km/h) and `engine_temp_c` (max 165°C) contain physically\n",
        "impossible values that are recoded to missing before imputation. `passenger_revenue_rwf` and\n",
        "`post_trip_incident_report` are **post-outcome** fields recorded only after the trip/incident is\n",
        "known, so they are excluded from prediction.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Pipeline design.** Numeric columns are median-imputed and standard-scaled; categorical columns\n",
        "are mode-imputed and one-hot encoded; all transformers are fit only on the training split. Data\n",
        "are split into train/validation/test (60/20/20) using the same stratified split for both targets\n",
        "so validation guides model/hyperparameter choice and the test set gives one untouched estimate.\n",
        "Two key leakage risks: (1) fitting the imputer/scaler/encoder on the full dataset before\n",
        "splitting would let validation/test statistics leak into training; (2) including\n",
        "`passenger_revenue_rwf` or `post_trip_incident_report` would let the model see information that\n",
        "only exists after the outcome occurred, inflating apparent performance unrealistically."
      ]
    },
