        "# 5. Ensemble learning — Required Text Cell\n",
        "\n",
        "**Bagging** trains many copies of a base learner on bootstrap resamples of the training data and\n",
        "averages/votes their predictions, which reduces variance for unstable learners like deep trees.\n",
        "**Random forests** add feature randomness (each split considers only a random subset of\n",
        "features), decorrelating the trees further and usually improving on plain bagging. **Boosting**\n",
        "builds trees sequentially, where each new tree focuses on correcting the errors of the previous\n",
        "ensemble, reducing bias by concentrating on hard cases. **Stacking** trains a meta-model on the\n",
        "out-of-fold predictions of several base models, learning how to best combine them rather than\n",
        "just averaging or voting. A single decision tree is **unstable**: small changes in training data\n",
        "can produce very different splits, which is exactly why bagging/random forests help (they trade\n",
        "a little bias for a large reduction in variance), while boosting deliberately trades some\n",
        "variance for lower bias. The key **leakage risk in stacking** is training the meta-model on\n",
        "base-model predictions made on the same rows the base models were trained on: those in-sample\n",
        "predictions are overly confident/accurate, so the meta-model would learn from unrealistically\n",
        "easy signals; using out-of-fold predictions (as `StackingClassifier(cv=5, ...)` does) avoids\n",
        "this by ensuring each base prediction used for meta-training came from a fold the base model did\n",
        "not see."
      ]
    },
