        "# 6. Clustering and dimensionality reduction — Required Text Cell\n",
        "\n",
        "**K-means** assigns each point to exactly one cluster (the nearest centroid) — a *hard*\n",
        "assignment — and iteratively updates centroids to the mean of their assigned points until\n",
        "convergence, which is a direct analogue of the EM algorithm's alternating\n",
        "assignment/update steps. A **Gaussian Mixture Model (GMM)** instead gives *soft* probabilistic\n",
        "membership of each point across all clusters, estimated by Expectation-Maximization: the E-step\n",
        "computes responsibility probabilities under the current parameters, and the M-step updates each\n",
        "component's mean/covariance/weight. **Silhouette** score measures how well-separated and compact\n",
        "clusters are using only the geometry of the data, while **BIC/AIC** score how well a probabilistic\n",
        "model (GMM) fits the data, penalising extra parameters — they give complementary, not identical,\n",
        "evidence for choosing k. The sensor variables are scaled because they are on very different units\n",
        "(temperature in °C, vibration in RMS units, a 0–100 GPS quality score) and unscaled distance-based\n",
        "methods would be dominated by whichever variable has the largest numeric range. **PCA** finds\n",
        "orthogonal directions of maximum variance and is computed via the **SVD** of the (centred) data\n",
        "matrix — the two are mathematically equivalent ways of reaching the same components. Cumulative\n",
        "explained variance tells us how many components are needed to retain most of the information.\n",
        "**MDS** instead tries to place points in 2D so that their pairwise distances match the original\n",
        "high-dimensional pairwise distances as closely as possible. Clusters found this way are\n",
        "**descriptive patterns** in the sensor data, not proven causal groups — route-days that cluster\n",
        "together share similar operating conditions, but the clustering itself says nothing about what\n",
        "*causes* those conditions."
      ]
