        "# 7. MLP and deep-learning foundations — Required Text Cell\n",
        "\n",
        "The MLP's input tensor has shape `(batch_size, n_features)`, where `n_features` is the number of\n",
        "columns produced by the preprocessor (numeric + one-hot columns) after fitting on the training\n",
        "data. A **perceptron** computes a weighted sum of its inputs plus a bias, then passes the result\n",
        "through a non-linear **activation** function; stacking many perceptrons in layers lets the network\n",
        "represent non-linear functions of the inputs. In the **forward pass**, inputs flow layer by layer\n",
        "to produce a prediction; a **loss** function compares that prediction with the true label; and\n",
        "**backpropagation** uses the chain rule to compute how much each weight contributed to the loss,\n",
        "so an optimiser (Adam) can adjust weights to reduce it. **ReLU** is used in hidden layers because\n",
        "it is cheap to compute and avoids the vanishing-gradient problem that saturating activations\n",
        "(like sigmoid) have deep in a network, while **sigmoid** is used on the output because it squashes\n",
        "the single output neuron into a valid 0–1 probability for binary classification. **Validation**\n",
        "data guide model/hyperparameter choices (e.g. when to stop training), while the **test set**\n",
        "gives one final, untouched performance estimate. In the learning curves, validation loss that\n",
        "rises while training loss keeps falling indicates **overfitting**; both curves staying high and\n",
        "flat indicates **underfitting**. **Dropout** randomly deactivates a fraction of neurons during\n",
        "training, forcing the network not to rely on any single neuron and acting as a regularizer\n",
        "alongside weight decay/early stopping. An MLP does not automatically beat simpler tabular models\n",
        "because tree ensembles and regularized linear models are often very competitive (or better) on\n",
        "small, structured/tabular datasets like this one, where the sample size is too small for a\n",
        "neural network's flexibility to be a decisive advantage."
      ]
