        "# 8. CNN, feature extraction and transfer learning — Required Text Cell\n",
        "\n",
        "An image batch tensor has shape `(batch, height, width, channels)` — here `(batch, 96, 96, 3)`\n",
        "for RGB images. A convolutional **filter/kernel** is a small learnable weight matrix slid across\n",
        "the image; each position produces one value in a **feature map**, and because the *same* filter\n",
        "weights are reused at every spatial position (**parameter sharing**), the network needs far fewer\n",
        "parameters than a fully-connected layer and can detect a pattern regardless of where it appears.\n",
        "**Pooling** (e.g. max-pooling) downsamples feature maps, reducing spatial size and giving some\n",
        "translation invariance. A **scratch CNN** learns its filters entirely from the small\n",
        "automobile/truck training set, starting from random weights. **Transfer learning** instead reuses\n",
        "filters already learned by MobileNetV2 on millions of diverse ImageNet images, keeping the base\n",
        "**frozen** so we only train a small classification head; this is efficient when the target\n",
        "dataset is small, though careful, low-learning-rate **fine-tuning** of the last base layers can\n",
        "sometimes squeeze out further gains once the head is trained. Near-duplicate images or frames\n",
        "from the same camera sequence must never be split across train/validation/test, because doing so\n",
        "would let the model \"recognise\" a near-identical image rather than genuinely generalise, inflating\n",
        "validation/test scores. There is a clear **domain shift** here: CIFAR-10 automobiles/trucks are\n",
        "small (32×32 upsampled), centred, single-object images taken from varied consumer photos, while\n",
        "real Rwandan road-camera imagery would show vehicles at varying distances/angles/lighting, partial\n",
        "occlusion, motion blur and multiple objects per frame — so this CIFAR-10 proxy is only useful for\n",
        "demonstrating the *pipeline*, not for claiming real-world road-camera performance. Validation and\n",
        "untouched test evidence must be reported separately because validation numbers can be\n",
        "(consciously or not) influenced by the choices made while iterating, while the test number is the\n",
        "one honest, single-use estimate of real generalisation."
      ]
