        "# 9. Final model card and recommendation — Required Text Cell\n",
        "\n",
        "**Demand model.** **Lasso** had the lowest validation MAE among OLS/PLS/Lasso and was selected\n",
        "as the final demand model. Its untouched-test performance was **MAE ~ 20.6 passengers,\n",
        "RMSE ~ 25.1, R-squared ~ 0.93** -- a small drop from validation, as expected on unseen data, but\n",
        "still a strong fit. Residuals scatter around zero without an obvious pattern, suggesting no\n",
        "strong remaining bias, though variance increases somewhat at higher demand levels.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Risk model.** Because `high_risk` is a rare outcome (only ~11% of route-days), the default\n",
        "0.50 threshold on logistic regression caught only some high-risk days on validation\n",
        "(recall ~ 0.29). **Lowering the threshold to 0.30** raised validation/test recall substantially\n",
        "(test recall ~ 0.73, precision ~ 0.15, F1 ~ 0.25, ROC-AUC ~ 0.68) at the direct cost of many more\n",
        "false alarms -- an explicit, deliberate trade-off given that a missed high-risk route-day is far\n",
        "costlier than an unnecessary inspection. The same cost-sensitive logic should guide the final\n",
        "deployed threshold for whichever classifier is chosen operationally.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Clustering / dimensionality reduction.** KMeans silhouette peaked at **k=2** (silhouette ~ 0.13),\n",
        "only modestly above k=3-5, and GMM's BIC/AIC also favoured the simplest 2-component solution --\n",
        "so route-days separate into two broad sensor-pattern groups rather than many fine-grained ones.\n",
        "Only **7 principal components** are needed to retain at least 80% of the sensor variance out of\n",
        "9 original sensor variables, showing the sensor readings are fairly correlated/redundant, though\n",
        "not collapsible to just 1-2 dimensions.\n",
        "\n",
        "**MLP / image models.** The tabular MLP's validation accuracy (~0.89) matched the \"always predict\n",
        "low risk\" baseline rate, with recall near zero at the default threshold -- the same class-imbalance\n",
        "effect seen in the classical classifiers, and a reminder that accuracy alone is a misleading\n",
        "metric here. This illustrates that extra depth does not guarantee a large gain on a modest,\n",
        "imbalanced tabular dataset. The frozen-MobileNetV2 transfer model and the scratch CNN are compared\n",
        "on validation accuracy/recall on the CIFAR-10 automobile/truck proxy task, and the better model by\n",
        "validation evidence is evaluated once on the untouched image test set (see Section 8 outputs,\n",
        "produced when this notebook is run in Google Colab with internet access for the CIFAR-10/ImageNet\n",
        "downloads).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Assumptions and uncertainty.** The synthetic dataset assumes stationarity (patterns learned\n",
        "from ~2026 route-days will continue to hold); sample sizes per route/district are modest, so\n",
        "metric estimates carry non-trivial sampling variance; and the CIFAR-10 image proxy is not a\n",
        "substitute for real road-camera footage.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Limitations.** Missing/impossible sensor values were imputed rather than verified against\n",
        "maintenance logs; categorical cleaning relied on a fixed mapping that may not generalise to new\n",
        "label variants; district-level sample sizes differ, risking uneven performance/fairness across\n",
        "districts; and CIFAR-10 has a substantial **domain shift** from real Rwandan road-camera imagery\n",
        "(controlled, centred, single-object photos vs. variable-angle, variable-lighting, multi-object\n",
        "camera footage), so image-model numbers should not be read as real-world accuracy.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Monitoring and retraining.** Track validation-style metrics on a rolling window of new route-days\n",
        "(MAE for demand; recall/precision/ROC-AUC for risk), monitor for data drift in traffic_index,\n",
        "occupancy_rate and sensor readings, and retrain when recall on recent high-risk days drops\n",
        "meaningfully or when new routes/vehicle types appear that were not in the training distribution.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Recommendations.** Use the demand model to inform route/vehicle scheduling and the risk model\n",
        "(with its lowered, recall-favouring threshold) to flag route-days for pre-emptive maintenance and\n",
        "safety inspection — but only as a decision-support signal alongside, not a replacement for,\n",
        "engineer judgement, since no single accuracy number establishes that a safety-relevant model is\n",
        "safe or ready to deploy unsupervised."
      ]
